    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d79">

                <pb facs="0242" n="110" xml:id="pg110"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source"> Leahy Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 79 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The President’s Chief of Staff</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Leahy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the President
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d79-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-06-20">20 June 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>At the joint request of General Marshall and Mr. Hopkins I have today sent the
                    following to Harriman:<anchor n="2" xml:id="d79-f2"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The President has in mind bringing his American Chiefs of Staff with him
                            to Berlin. Please ascertain Stalin’s reaction to having the Chiefs of
                            Staff come with the President, you Harriman having in mind the possible
                            Japanese reaction.</p>
                        <p>Early information on this question is desired.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Both Marshall and Hopkins doubt the advisability and see no necessity of a staff
                    meeting in Germany at this time and fear that Stalin would not like it.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d79-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d79-f1-content">
